<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔφρων</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰφρ</span>-, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, both in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cheerful, merry</i>, of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ πέρ τις . . δαίνυται εὔφρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.99
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.531
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἶλαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					5.38
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νως</span>
			<i>with good cheer</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>P.</u>
				10.40
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>cheering, making glad</i> or <i>merry</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.246
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					6.115
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔφρων πόνος εὖ τελέσασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					806
				</span></i>
			 codd.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ φέγγος εὖφρον</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1577
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοαὶ εὔφρονες Ἀργείοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					420
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): neut. pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔφροσιν
				δεδεγμένη,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφροσύναις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				632
			</span></i> (s.v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>kindly, gracious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεὸς εὔ. εἴη εὐχαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					4.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				772
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				705
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1411
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαῖαν ἀνθρώποισι καὶ εὔφρονα μήλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					7.63
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἥδ᾽ ὁμιλία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					1030
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῆφον δ᾽ εὔφρον᾽ ἔθεντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					640
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίφρονος</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.29
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				351
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of sound mind, reasonable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					1.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔφημος, πῶς εὔφρον᾽
				εἴπω</span>
			; <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				88
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ αὖ τόδ᾽ εὖφρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					378
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
